<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Acceptable use — Cadastre</title><meta name="description" content="The acceptable use and access attestation for Cadastre restricted research materials."/><meta name="robots" content="noindex"/></head><body><header class="site-header shell legal-header"><a href="/" class="wordmark">cadastre<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a><a href="/#access" class="header-access">Research access ↗</a></header><main class="shell legal-page"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH ACCESS POLICY</p><h1>Accountable access.<br/>Legitimate research.</h1><p class="legal-version">Policy version {AUP_VERSION}</p><p>Cadastre makes its code, schemas, and source index public. Access to restricted specimens and research deliveries requires organizational review, domain control, and an explicit attestation.</p><h2>The attestation</h2><p class="legal-policy">{AUP_TEXT}</p><h2>What access means</h2><p>A request begins in pending review. Demonstrating domain control establishes control of a domain; it does not establish an organization’s legal identity, an applicant’s authority, or eligibility. Organization and authority review are separate requirements.</p><h2>Research limits</h2><p>Extracted specimens, normalized geometry, crop proposals, and source observations are reference research. They do not independently establish the authenticity of a presented document, the completeness of a jurisdiction’s design coverage, or calibrated physical measurements.</p><h2>Current policy</h2><p>The application shows the current policy before submission. Your request records its version and an attestation receipt. The machine-readable current policy is available at <a href="/v1/policy">/v1/policy</a>.</p><p><a href="/">← Return to Cadastre</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a></p></main></body></html>
